  "artifact_src": "\"\"\"probe.py\n\nAs of 2026-08-23, this script reads every ``*.json`` file directly inside a\ngiven directory (non-recursively), collects the top-level ``cost_usd`` value\nfrom each file that has one, and writes ``summary.json`` in the current\nworking directory with the total and mean of those values, plus the\nresolved source directory path.\n\nAs of 2026-08-23, see eval/IMPROVEMENTS.md for background on this tool.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef main():\n    source_dir = Path(sys.argv[1]).resolve()\n\n    values = []\n    for path in sorted(source_dir.glob(\"*.json\")):\n        if not path.is_file():\n            continue\n        with open(path, \"r\") as f:\n            data = json.load(f)\n        if isinstance(data, dict) and \"cost_usd\" in data:\n            values.append(data[\"cost_usd\"])\n\n    total = sum(values)\n    mean = total / len(values) if values else 0.0\n\n    summary = {\n        \"total\": total,\n        \"mean\": mean,\n        \"source_dir\": str(source_dir),\n    }\n\n    with open(\"summary.json\", \"w\") as f:\n        json.dump(summary, f)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n",
